{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA evidence (2026-08-28, read-only investigation on i-00880b2c7f13527c5)\n\nConfirms this ticket and localizes it precisely: **the app already serves the document; only the nginx edge fails to route it.**\n\nProbed from the box, same moment:\n\n    app  (direct, http://<container-ip>:8091)\n      /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp   -> 200\n      /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource       -> 404\n      /mcp/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource   -> 404\n\n    edge (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com)\n      /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp   -> 404\n      /mcp/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource   -> 404\n\n401 challenge verbatim from the edge:\n\n    www-authenticate: Bearer error=\"invalid_token\", error_description=\"Authentication required\",\n      resource_metadata=\"https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp\"\n\n### Mechanism\n\n`infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template` declares only `location = /mcp/` (:157), `location = /mcp` (:178)\nand the prefix `location /mcp` (:195) for the MCP app, plus `location /.well-known/acme-challenge/`\n(:66). `/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp` matches none of them, so it falls through to\n`location /` (:224) -> `proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8080` (Gerrit), which 404s. The live\n`/etc/nginx/conf.d/rebar.conf` matches the template, so this reproduces on every deploy.\n\nThis narrows the ticket's AC#1: the fix is a one-location edge route, not a new server feature —\nthe resource-server metadata document exists and returns 200 on the app.\n\n### Not the cause of the 2026-08-28 401 outage\n\nInvestigated alongside a live \"MCP auth suddenly 401s\" report. Independent: that report's root cause\nwas a client-side unexpanded `${MCP_CLIENT_PAT_COPILOT}` placeholder in `~/.copilot/mcp-config.json`\n(`rebar doctor` reports it as `copilot [error] pat-unresolvable`). Static-bearer clients never fetch\n`resource_metadata`, and a probe with the real PAT returned `initialize` -> 200 while the edge\nstill 404s this path. So this stays P3, and it is not a client-recovery blocker today."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787941707829188943,"uuid":"19731771-34ae-4082-b143-e18891ea4f36"}